# Project stack

- React 19, Next.js 16 (App Router only).
- TypeScript 6.0 (strict mode). Do not use syntax that is only available in TS 7 unless it compiles under 6.0.
- Plain CSS via CSS Modules (`.module.css`). No Tailwind, styled-components, SCSS, or inline styles.
- MobX 7 + mobx-react-lite 5 for global state. React 19, functional components only.
- Vitest 5 for tests. Tests live next to components: `ComponentName.test.tsx`.

# Project layout

```
app/                        # Repository root (Next.js App Router)
├── layout.tsx
├── page.tsx
├── api/
└── ...

src/
├── components/             # Reusable UI without business logic (ui/, layout/)
├── features/               # Business features (each self-contained)
│   └── feature-name/
│       ├── components/
│       ├── hooks/
│       └── stores/
├── stores/                 # Global stores (RootStore, StoreContext, useStore)
├── lib/                    # Utilities, helpers, API clients
├── types/                  # Shared TypeScript types
└── styles/                 # Global styles (if needed)

public/                     # Next.js static assets (favicon, images)
```

Placement rules:

- **app/** at the project root (not `src/app/`) — routing only: page, layout, loading, error, route handlers. Files stay thin: import from `src/features/` or `src/components/` and render.
- **src/features/** — business logic. A feature must not import another feature’s internals; shared code goes in `components/`, `lib/`, or `types/`.
- **src/components/** — reusable UI. If a component is needed by a single feature, it lives inside that feature.
- Stores: global in `src/stores/`, feature-local in `features/*/stores/`.
- PWA (manifest, service worker, install prompt) is not implemented yet — do not add without a dedicated task.

# Component folder structure

Each component lives in its own folder named after the component (e.g. `Button/` for `Button.tsx`). Everything for that component goes inside:

ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx          # Component code
├── ComponentName.module.css   # Styles (sibling of the component file)
├── ComponentName.test.tsx     # Tests (sibling of the component file)
├── assets/                    # Static files (images, icons, fonts, JSON)
│   └── ...
└── ...                        # Other component artifacts (subcomponents, hooks used only here)

Rules:

- The folder name matches the component (PascalCase).
- Styles and tests sit next to the component file, NOT in `assets/`.
- Static files (images, SVG, fonts, JSON) go in `assets/` inside the component folder.
- Import static assets with a relative path: `./assets/icon.svg`.
- Subcomponents used only by this component may live in the same folder.

# Forbidden

- NEVER use Pages Router (`pages/`), `getServerSideProps`, or `getStaticProps`.
- NEVER use class components. Only functions with hooks.
- NEVER use `any` in TypeScript.
- NEVER create `.css` files without the `.module` suffix.
- NEVER use `Provider`, `inject`, or `MobXProviderContext` from `mobx-react` or `mobx-react-lite` — they were removed in MobX 7 / mobx-react-lite 5. Use `React.createContext` for the store provider.
- NEVER put business logic or markup in `app/` — only import and render components from `features/`.
- NEVER put styles or tests in `assets/` — they belong next to the component file.
